  "title": "The Double Cap Conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture The largest measure of a Lebesgue measurable subset of the unit sphere of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ containing no pair of orthogonal vectors is attained by two open caps of geodesic radius $\\pi/4$ around the north and south poles.",
